    "created_at": "2016-11-29T16:10:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-29T16:10:16Z",
    "body": "@foolip, sure - I can undertake that. \r\n\r\nRe: your questions...\r\n\r\n- Removing a TextTrack object that comes from a track element removes the element (existing behavior).\r\n- I'm ok with throwing an exception when there's an attempt to remove in-band tracks added by the browser. Browsers that add in-band tracks remove them when the media changes, so there's never a need, really, to remove them programmatically.  At JW Player, we use a custom property to identify tracks added programmatically so we can target them for \"cleanup\" before changing media.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/263614802/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
